  "generateLearnedAbilities": {
    "custom": "---\n---\n# Learned Abilities — Aerfála Custom\n\nWhen the player gains a new ability through leveling, training, or story events:\n\n## Multiple Cheat Skills\nThe player can have up to THREE cheat skills, chosen at character creation. All of them evolve — each cheat skill with the player's base trait develops its own T1, T2, and T3 ability chain. When a player gains an Evolved Power Tier trait, ALL of their cheat skills that have evolved abilities at that tier become available. Do not gate evolved abilities behind additional triggers; if the player has the tier trait and the base cheat skill, the evolved ability is available. Players who pick multiple cheat skills are choosing a power fantasy — let them be powerful. Players who pick one are choosing a focused narrative. Both are valid.\n\n## New Abilities on Level Up\n- Class abilities should feel like natural progressions of the player's combat style — a Berserker gains rage-adjacent skills, a Sage gains spell school expansions\n- Cheat skill abilities should evolve as the player's understanding of their power deepens — an Appraisal user learns to read deeper, a Heal user learns to cure more complex conditions. These are NEW ABILITIES within the SAME cheat skill, not new cheat skills.\n- Abilities gained from NPCs should reflect the teacher — learning from Ithilwen teaches precision, learning from Brunhilde teaches force\n- Name the ability something the character would actually call it — not \"Ability #7\" but \"Crimson Edge\" or \"Spirit Sight\" or \"Second Wind\"\n- Every new ability should have a scene where the player discovers or learns it — not a menu unlock, but a story moment\n\n## Only offer the character's OWN build\nWhen offering abilities to learn or unlock (including level-up ability points), ONLY offer abilities that belong to the character's actual class/trait build. If an ability's requirements include a `trait` the character does NOT have, it is OFF-LIMITS — never list it, never let it be purchased. Do not present the full cross-class ability catalogue (Saint sets, god/demon-lord, ranger, hunter, kami, etc.); a character may only learn abilities their own traits grant or gate, plus universal untyped ones. Treat a class trait as the hard key to that class's abilities."
